From 587b769f486caedb3f45ef75640e46b4c306b931 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:46:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: working saves (GS interrupts, GS->memory downloads,
 device latency, card fixes)

Zettai's save/load now works end to end (save screen with a captured
thumbnail, files on the host card, Continue/Load restores the scene).

- GS SIGNAL/FINISH raise INTC cause 0 on the 0->1 CSR edge when unmasked in
  IMR, delivered through the scheduler after ~2000 EE cycles. Transfers are
  synchronous here, but the thumbnail capture starts the transfer and then
  calls SleepThread, relying on the hardware delay before the interrupt.
- VIF1 DMA with CHCR.DIR = 0 fills memory from the GS local->host transfer;
  its completion interrupt is likewise delivered after a size-based latency
  (EeEventType::Dmac now dispatches DMAC handlers).
- Memory card: opens without access bits (CREAT alone) are read/write, and
  MCSERV GetDir returns the host directory listing (the game verifies saves
  with it); card requests carry six arguments.
- Diagnostics: GA2_DMA_TRACE (non-chain GIF/VIF1 starts, GS interrupts),
  GA2_MC_TRACE, GA2_PAD_TRACE, thread/interrupt syscalls in
  GA2_SYSCALL_TRACE, EE thread states in GA2_WATCHDOG, several dump ranges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
